# AI Orchestration Architecture

Version: 1.0

Status: Canonical

Owner: LESOM Dynamics

Project: CodeAtlas

---

# Overview

The AI Orchestration Layer is responsible for coordinating all AI reasoning within CodeAtlas.

Rather than relying on a single general-purpose assistant, CodeAtlas is composed of specialized agents that collaborate to understand, reason about, validate, document, and evolve software systems.

Each agent has a narrowly defined responsibility.

No agent performs tasks outside its domain.

The AI Orchestrator plans work, delegates execution, aggregates outputs, resolves conflicts, and presents unified results to users.

---

# Design Principles

Specialization over Generalization

Every agent should solve one problem exceptionally well.

Deterministic Context

Agents receive structured architectural context instead of raw repositories whenever possible.

Tool First

Agents should use tools before relying on language reasoning.

Explainability

Every recommendation must include reasoning.

Approval

No agent may modify repositories without explicit approval.

Composable Workflows

Agents may invoke other agents.

Stateless Execution

Agents remain stateless.

Persistent knowledge belongs to the Knowledge Graph.

